WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.381
Azure credentials and sessions are
sensitive operational authority.

2
00:00:07.461 --> 00:00:13.540
They may exist as local Azure CLI login
sessions, token caches,

3
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:20.272
service principal secrets, certificates,
federated credentials,

4
00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:27.577
managed identities, environment variables,
CI/CD service connections,

5
00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:29.607
or temporary files.

6
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:37.256
The script does not need to print a token
for that token to define what the script

7
00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:38.024
can do.

8
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:45.445
Long-lived static secrets should be
minimized where better options exist.

9
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:52.865
Managed identity, workload identity,
federation, short-lived sessions,

10
00:00:52.945 --> 00:01:00.055
and approved secret stores can reduce risk
when they fit the environment.

11
00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:04.264
They do not remove the need for
validation,

12
00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:12.258
but they can reduce reliance on durable
secrets and improve governance of runtime

13
00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.140
access.

14
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:20.790
Scripts should check whether the required
login context is available without

15
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.540
printing tokens or sensitive values.

16
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:32.533
Avoid exposing secrets, token-derived
values, service principal credentials,

17
00:01:32.613 --> 00:01:37.889
full environments, debug traces, or
support bundles.

18
00:01:37.969 --> 00:01:43.589
CI/CD masking is useful, but it is not a
complete boundary.

19
00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:49.289
Sensitive values can still leak through
command echoing,

20
00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:56.365
transformed output, temporary files,
artifacts, or verbose tool logs.

21
00:01:56.445 --> 00:02:04.932
Credential handling includes rotation,
revocation, ownership, and lifetime limits.

22
00:02:05.012 --> 00:02:12.237
Teams should know how to disable an
exposed service principal credential,

23
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:19.886
revoke a connection, expire a session,
review a managed identity assignment,

24
00:02:19.966 --> 00:02:24.439
and determine which jobs used the
credential.

25
00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:31.745
Secure Azure CLI automation treats
credentials as scoped and reviewable,

26
00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:35.380
not permanent background plumbing.
